AB  - This paper explores a comprehensive approach to addressing the challenges of global population aging through the integration of cutting-edge technologies in smart elderly care. The study focuses on key aspects such as multi-point navigation, IoT communication, speech recognition, autonomous navigation, and elderly monitoring, employing advanced sensors and the Robot Operating System (ROS). Intelligent elderly care robots equipped with cameras, lidar, and IMU sensors ensure precise navigation, while Home Assistant and ZigBee2 facilitate IoT communication for smart home integration. The research also introduces a fall detection system based on the YOLOv5 algorithm. Despite current technological limitations, the paper emphasizes the significant potential of these innovations in enhancing the quality of life for the elderly, highlighting the importance of future advancements and user feedback for further refinement.
