AB  - This paper introduces a pipeline crawling robot that enhances navigation in complex pipeline systems by integrating Proportional-Integral-Derivative (PID) control with the Rapidly- Exploring Random Tree (RRT) algorithm. Traditional inspection robots struggle with sharp turns, steep climbs, and obstacles in confined spaces. By employing the RRT algorithm, the robot efficiently plans paths to navigate obstacles, tight bends, and vertical sections. The PID control system ensures stable and precise movements across varying pipeline configurations, preventing slippage and loss of balance. Equipped with multi-jointed legs, the robot dynamically adjusts its posture to maintain traction and overcome obstacles. Simulations demonstrate that this design outperforms traditional models, effectively reducing inspection time and energy consumption. This approach offers a robust and adaptable solution that significantly enhances performance and operational efficiency in industrial pipeline inspections.
